-title>3-D conformal treatment of prostate cancer to 74 Gy vs. high-dose-rate brachytherapy boost: a cross-sectional quality-of-life survey</article-title><source>Acta Oncol</source><year>2006</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>708</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/02841860600710913</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16938814</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Wahlgren</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nilsson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lennern&#x000e4;s</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Brandberg</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><article-title>Promising long-term health-related quality of life after high-dose-rate brachytherapy boost for localized prostate cancer</article-title><source>Int J Radiat Oncol Biol Phys</source><year>2007</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>662</fpage><lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17499452</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>